{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1115435-the-fall-of-arcadia-and-the-return-of-the-tuatha-playable-gods","id":1115435,"title":"The Fall of Arcadia and the return of the Tuatha: Playable Gods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-13T02:17:53-07:00","id":1115435,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> The Fall of Arcadia and the return of the Tuatha: Playable Gods","content":"So I have an idea for the coming Fimbul Winter. So lets say some changeling hero manages to actually find his way into Fabled Arcadia. This brings Winter to Faery, something the Fae knew, and the Tuatha were awaiting it. They enact a final rite of spring, and rather than succumb to Winter, or possibly even the Fomorians they are reborn upon the Earth. Perhaps this is somewhere between Arcadian Sidhe stealing bodies and the Changeling way ritual, depending on your taste. Was this preventable? Was this expected to happen?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So now the Tuatha are born into new bodies. Way back before the Time of Judgement ended Revised Era World of Darkness, I predicted we would get two gamelines, one about Aliens and one about Demigods. Then Time of Judgement happened and we got Scion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So I\u2019m thinking this would be for a chronicle were all the players are newborn gods, or playing as changelings in a world where the Tuatha are being reborn, but they are NPCs. Depending on how you want the timeline to play out this could have been Prince David who sought Arcadia in his disappearance or hell it could be anyone, House Balor, or even a Nunnehi out to save the Higher Hunting grounds by heralding winter.<br /> <br /> <br /> So I\u2019m thinking each of these Godlings would be similar to changelings, having legacies (though maybe give them special God legacies), glamour and banality. But their Glamour is more potent, so maybe they have temporary glamour worth their permanent rating squared. They can perhaps gain some sort of mythic Attributes, basically linking their Glamour rating to specific attributes, boosting it by their glamour rating, perhaps limiting the number of attributes by glamour. This would be something it would be fruitful to talk about.<br /> <br /> <br /> Probably they should also get something to bolster their Unleashings, maybe counting their glamour as twice as high, or maybe allowing Arts to go up to 6 an arch rating boosting unleashings.<br /> <br /> <br /> Modify each God individually, using the Kith Creation rules, based on the legend of the God they were in a past life, except perhaps have double the boons of a standard Changeling kith, with the fact that they grow more godlike the deeper into the dreaming they go.<br /> <br /> <br /> And each God also is a house unto themselves, giving them a Unique House Oath and Boon (Perhaps an extra strong one) and the ability to adopt others into their house. They also have the power to create new changeling souls, in the form of both full on creation, as well as good old fashion procreation with just about anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> At Glamour 6+ their traits are not 5 anymore and are limited to their Glamour. They must now start to decide if they will choose to stay a being of flesh, and better able to walk the world of man, or achieve apotheosis and become a being of the Dreaming/Spirit World.<br /> <br /> Perhaps this is a cycle, and older gods reach a point where they are reborn, their previous legends somewhat defining their new lives, in the form of their Birthrights/Boons and bonus/Favored Arts.<br /> <br /> <br /> So maybe Gods have Access to the Arts of Changelings, Splinters of Inanimae, and the Alchemies of the Hsien, and perhaps even the Dark Age powers (Still need to read that). And depending on their nature they will favore one method of power over the others. Or hell let you just take any and favor like three or four or something. They are just limited in favoring something tied to their past life. Or maybe the Gods/Tuatha are split along who they are the progenitors of. Kith/Gallain are most Gods, and Inanimae are tied to some gods or maybe Titans/Fomorians, like Jord having Stone Slinters and the like. <br /> <br /> So maybe they start like changeling but more options, and more supernatural points. And Gods in general have more Background points, or at least maybe give them more Treasures as they are reborn tied to their Panoply. And they have a greatly enhanced lifespan, until they achieve Apotheosis and become immortals.<br /> <br /> This should be discussed. Thoughts?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T17:52:07-07:00","id":1115735,"title":"","content":"Personally I don't like the idea of playing such powerful creatures, but that's just me. I had the Scion line of books and didn't like it when you got to near godhood level. I think it's more interesting to play characters who have to take big risks with their lives and are uncertain about the success of their actions. I also felt the same way when old D&amp;D introduced the mega-level immortals setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T01:09:02-07:00","id":1115839,"title":"","content":"Your Tuatha godlings look very much like the Fae in Changeling: the Lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T10:41:46-07:00","id":1141809,"title":"","content":"To me, Tuathans <i>do</i> have stats, but these are monstrously, obscenely epic stats. In my games, they're NPC-only, and for good reason!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T14:27:52-07:00","id":1141897,"title":"","content":"I could see a demi god kith existing, probably as a proper Gallian who harvest glamour through cult personality and having a cult. There was a pooka in the kithbook who did just that, started a new age hippy commune that cut off its inhabitants from the outside world and all followed him religiously along with tenets of the faith. I would hate to make a PC a straight up god, but them reincarnating as a hero/Demi working his way back into the dreaming grace. They could have a fragility that is more or less chimera magnet and the hubris of a would be god sets in. As for magic at their disposal, possibly base that on the culture they come from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}